<title>UNITED NATIONS: Albright-Iraq makes outrageous demands on oil deal.</title>
<headline>Albright-Iraq makes outrageous demands on oil deal.</headline>
<dateline>UNITED NATIONS 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States Ambassador to the United States said on Friday that Iraq was making &quot;outrageous demands&quot; on how a deal to partially lift a bar on oil exports should be implemented.</p>
<p>Ambassador Madeleine Albright, speaking after the U.N. Security Council voted at its regular 60-day review to hold in place broad sanctions against Iraq, said: &quot;Iraq has made outrageous demands outside of the terms of the memorandum of understanding.&quot;</p>
</text>
